  "purpose": "Validate a selective inline AVX2/FMA NHWC pointwise kernel that removes the per-six-row Windows vector save/restore and tile-return boundary without changing packed weights or arithmetic order.",
  "status": "completed_fixed_scope",
  "assessment": "Retained only the short-reduction inline kernel. Final kernel medians were 1.97-3.92% lower, but all final observed sample ranges overlap. Small and Medium full-page medians were 0.83% and 0.36% higher respectively, also within overlapping ranges. These bounded measurements do not establish an end-to-end dense-page latency improvement. The new path is a modest kernel-level optimization candidate, not a claim that the dominant large-channel recognition work has been accelerated.",
